.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the miscutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width readahead
.It Nm adjtimex
Read or set kernel time variables, through
.Xr adjtimex 2 ;
an offset steps the clock, which has no slew.
.It Nm ascii
Print an ASCII table.
.It Nm bc
Calculate with arbitrary precision.
.It Nm chat
Exchange expect-send argument pairs with a modem on standard input and output.
.It Nm crond
Run scheduled commands from crontabs.
.It Nm dc
Calculate using reverse Polish notation, with operands before operators.
Arithmetic operators are
.Ql + ,
.Ql - ,
.Ql * ,
.Ql / ,
.Ql % ,
and
.Ql ^ ;
.Ql ~
divides with remainder,
.Ql |
performs modular exponentiation, and
.Ql v
computes the square root.
.It Nm devmem
Read or write a physical address through
.Pa /dev/mem .
Rach2 has no
.Pa /dev/mem ,
so this applet cannot access physical memory here.
.It Nm hexedit
Edit a file in hexadecimal.
.It Nm less
View files, or standard input, one screen at a time.
.It Nm lsscsi
Display SCSI bus and device information from
.Pa /sys/bus/scsi/devices ,
which Rach2 does not have; nothing is listed.
.It Nm makedevs
Make the directories a device table names under
.Ar rootdir
and set the owners and modes of its entries.
The table's regular files must exist already, and its device nodes and
FIFOs cannot be made, since Rach2 has no
.Fn mknod
system call.
.It Nm microcom
Copy bytes from standard input to
.Ar TTY
and from
.Ar TTY
to standard output.
.It Nm mim
Run a script from a specification file with Makefile-like syntax.
.It Nm mt
Control a magnetic tape drive.
Rach2 has no tape devices and does not implement their requests.
.It Nm readahead
Preload files into the page cache, through
.Xr readahead 2 .
Rach2's page cache fills a page when a read first asks for it, so the call
starts no reads: the applet succeeds and preloads nothing.
.It Nm runlevel
Find the previous and current system runlevels.
Print
.Ql unknown
if the utmp file does not exist or contains no runlevel record.
.It Nm rx
Receive a file using the XMODEM protocol.
.It Nm setfattr
Set or remove extended file attributes, through
.Xr setxattr 2
and
.Xr removexattr 2 .
No file system of Rach2 stores extended attributes, so both calls fail with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
on an existing file and the applet fails.
.It Nm setserial
Print or set serial port parameters.
Rach2 does not implement the serial configuration requests.
.It Nm strings
Display printable strings in binary files.
.It Nm time
Run
.Ar PROG
and display its resource usage when it exits.
.It Nm tree
List files and directories in a tree structure.
.It Nm ts
Copy standard input to standard output, adding a timestamp to each line.
.It Nm ttysize
Print the dimensions of the terminal, asked of standard input, then
standard output, then standard error; 80 by 24 when none answers.
.It Nm volname
Show the CD volume name of
.Ar DEVICE ;
the default device is
.Pa /dev/cdrom .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss adjtimex
.Bl -tag -width "-f FREQ"
.It Fl q
Suppress output.
.It Fl o Ar OFF
Set the time offset in microseconds.
.It Fl f Ar FREQ
Set the frequency adjustment in integer kernel units; 65536 is one
part per million.
.It Fl t Ar TICK
Set the microseconds per tick, usually 10000.
Positive
.Fl t
or
.Fl f
values make the clock run faster.
.El
.Ss crond
.Bl -tag -width "-L FILE"
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground.
.It Fl b
Run in the background; this is the default.
.It Fl S
Log to syslog; this is the default.
.It Fl l Ar N
Set the log level.
Level 0 is most verbose; the default is 8.
.It Fl d Ar N
Set the log level and log to standard error.
.It Fl L Ar FILE
Log to
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl c Ar DIR
Use
.Ar DIR
for crontabs; the default is
.Pa /var/spool/cron/crontabs .
.El
.Ss devmem
.Ar ADDRESS
is the physical address to access.
.Ar WIDTH
is the width in bits, such as 8 or 16.
If
.Ar VALUE
is given, write that value.
.Ss less
.Bl -tag -width "-M, -m"
.It Fl E
Quit when the end of a file is reached.
.It Fl F
Quit if the whole file fits on the first screen.
.It Fl I
Ignore case in all searches.
.It Fl M , Fl m
Display a status line with line numbers and the percentage through the file.
.It Fl N
Prefix each line with its number.
.It Fl S
Truncate long lines.
.It Fl R
Remove color escape codes from input.
.It Fl ~
Suppress tildes displayed past the end of the file.
.El
.Ss makedevs
.Fl d Ar device_table
selects the device table.
Each entry has the form:
.Dl name type mode uid gid major minor start inc count
.Ar name
is the file name;
.Ar uid
and
.Ar gid
are its user and group IDs.
The
.Ar type
field is one of:
.Bl -tag -width f -compact
.It Cm f
Regular file.
.It Cm d
Directory.
.It Cm c
Character device.
.It Cm b
Block device.
.It Cm p
FIFO, or named pipe.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ar major , minor , start , inc ,
and
.Ar count
fields apply to device special files.
A
.Ql -
may be used for a blank field.
.Ss microcom
.Bl -tag -width "-t TIMEOUT"
.It Fl d Ar DELAY
Before sending each next byte, wait up to
.Ar DELAY
milliseconds for terminal output.
.It Fl t Ar TIMEOUT
Exit if both standard input and the terminal are silent for
.Ar TIMEOUT
milliseconds.
.It Fl s Ar SPEED
Set the serial line speed.
.It Fl X
Disable the special meanings of NUL and Ctrl-X from standard input.
.El
.Ss mim
.Fl f Ar FILE
selects the specification file; the default is
.Pa Mimfile .
.Ss mt
.Fl f Ar DEVICE
selects the tape device.
The operation codes are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bsf bsfm bsr bss datacompression drvbuffer eof eom erase
fsf fsfm fsr fss load lock mkpart nop offline ras1 ras2
ras3 reset retension rewind rewoffline seek setblk setdensity
setpart tell unload unlock weof wset
.Ed
.Ss setfattr
.Bl -tag -width "-v VALUE"
.It Fl h
Do not follow symbolic links.
.It Fl x Ar ATTR
Remove the attribute.
.It Fl n Ar ATTR
Set the attribute to
.Ar VALUE .
.It Fl v Ar VALUE
Specify the value; the default is an empty value.
.El
.Ss setserial
.Bl -tag -width "-a"
.It Fl a
Print all parameters.
.It Fl b
Print a summary.
.It Fl G
Print parameters in a form accepted by
.Nm setserial .
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl z
Clear serial flags before setting them.
.It Fl g
Treat all operands as device names.
.El
.Pp
The following parameters take an argument:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
port irq divisor uart baud_base close_delay closing_wait
.Ed
.Pp
The following flags can be disabled by prefixing the name with
.Ql ^ :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fourport auto_irq skip_test sak session_lockout pgrp_lockout
callout_nohup split_termios hup_notify low_latency
.Ed
.Pp
Other parameters are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
autoconfig spd_normal spd_hi spd_vhi spd_shi spd_warp spd_cust
.Ed
.Pp
The argument to
.Cm uart
is one of:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
unknown 8250 16450 16550 16550A Cirrus 16650 16650V2 16750
16950 16954 16654 16850 RSA NS16550A XSCALE RM9000 OCTEON AR7
U6_16550A
.Ed
.Ss time
.Bl -tag -width "-o FILE"
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl p
Use POSIX output format.
.It Fl f Ar FMT
Use a custom output format.
.It Fl o Ar FILE
Write the result to
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl a
Append the result instead of overwriting the output file.
.El
.Ss ts
.Bl -tag -width "-s"
.It Fl s
Print the time elapsed since
.Nm ts
started.
.It Fl i
Print time since the previous line.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/spool/cron/crontabs
.It Pa /var/spool/cron/crontabs
Default crontab directory for
.Nm crond .
.It Pa Mimfile
Default specification file for
.Nm mim .
.It Pa /dev/mem
Physical memory device used by
.Nm devmem ;
absent on Rach2.
.It Pa /dev/cdrom
Default device for
.Nm volname .
.El
